# The first loop on the woodcutter layout: the castle, the flag and road to the hut's flag, and the woodcutter's finished hut
# (the layout's finished-building entry stands it with its worker), then fast-forwards until a log has reached the castle.
# Run it on the layout: sh tools/play-run.sh first-loop --layout layouts/woodcutter.jsonc --fps 10
# The castle stands at 10,10, so its flag is at 11,11; the road runs three steps east to the hut's flag at 14,11, and the
# woodcutter's hut stands at 13,10, north-west of it.
wait 0.3
dump castle
shot castle

expect-at 14 11 flag
expect-at 12 11 road
expect-at 13 10 building
expect logs = 4
dump woodcutter
shot woodcutter

# The castle starts with 4 logs; a fifth is the woodcutter's.
fast-forward until logs >= 5 max 20000
wait 0.3
expect logs >= 5
dump log
shot log
